So Orcrist and Sting are now chaotic . . . joy.

Chaotics need a new artifact so that they can have two good artifacts
as well. Lawfuls have Excaliber and Grayswandir, neutrals have the
vorpal sword and Mjolnir.  Chaotics have Stormbringer.

Here is what I propose: a dancing sword
Have a sword that, every x many turns of battle, leaps from your grasp
	and fights any creature within two squares of you (ie, it
	stays in squares ajacent to you) for y many turns, then
	returns to your hand and pushes what-ever weapon you are
	holding out of your hand. (not making you drop it, just into
	your pack)
- Or perhaps it could be an artifact that attacks when you invoke it.
- Perhaps it fights until you grasp it again, but if you take to long,
	it turns against you.
- Weilding it could cause conflict.  
- Its damage could be as if you were weilding it.  
  . if this makes it too powerful, there could be penalties for
	enchanting it (like magic bane) so that it is independant for
	shorter and shorter amounts of time the more you enchant it .
- Rather than blasting people with power, it could attack a person
	until they grasped it.
- It would make amusing bones levels:
	"The Dancing Sword hits. The dancing sword hits."

It would take a lot of coding (although it could be tied in with the
code for pets) but I think it would be worth it.


